1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:09,000
High on a stone beam in an Egyptian temple, about three thousand three hundred years old, there is a carving that looks like a helicopter.

2
00:00:09,466 --> 00:00:10,329
Not roughly.

3
00:00:10,329 --> 00:00:13,924
It has a rotor on top, a cockpit, and a long tail.

4
00:00:13,924 --> 00:00:18,166
Next to it, people see a submarine, a tank and a jet plane.

5
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:26,862
For more than twenty five years, it has been one of the internet's favourite proofs that ancient Egypt had flying machines.

6
00:00:26,862 --> 00:00:28,199
Or visitors who did.

7
00:00:28,666 --> 00:00:33,907
So tonight we treat it the way a forensic lab treats a suspicious document.

8
00:00:33,907 --> 00:00:35,444
A questioned document.

9
00:00:35,444 --> 00:00:39,566
Every claim is an exhibit, and every exhibit gets examined.

10
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:40,540
Intake.

11
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,060
Photo authentication.

12
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,290
Chain of custody.

13
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:44,014
Two hands.

14
00:00:44,014 --> 00:00:44,811
The filler.

15
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:45,679
The reading.

16
00:00:45,679 --> 00:00:47,199
Comparison specimens.

17
00:00:51,666 --> 00:00:55,245
Then a lab report, with a scorecard and a verdict.

18
00:00:55,245 --> 00:00:59,468
Genuine aircraft, or something stranger and far more human.

19
00:00:59,468 --> 00:01:00,899
Let's open the file.

20
00:01:01,366 --> 00:01:05,136
Exhibit A arrived, like so many mysteries, by email.

21
00:01:05,136 --> 00:01:13,400
In the mid nineteen nineties, photos of the beam were passed around on mailing lists about U F Os and archaeology.

22
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:23,133
The picture was striking: a neat little helicopter, perfectly outlined, sitting in a line of hieroglyphs as if somebody had carved it from life.

23
00:01:23,599 --> 00:01:31,506
Beside it, other shapes: a long one that looks like a submarine or an airship, and a boxy one that looks like a tank.

24
00:01:31,506 --> 00:01:33,533
Below, something like a plane.

25
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,878
The theories followed fast.

26
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:37,200
Egypt had aircraft.

27
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,313
Or Atlantis did.

28
00:01:38,313 --> 00:01:45,200
Or visitors from the stars showed the priests their machines, and the priests carved what they saw.

29
00:01:45,666 --> 00:01:48,355
Television documentaries picked it up.

30
00:01:48,355 --> 00:01:49,699
Websites copied it.

31
00:01:49,699 --> 00:01:56,066
In twenty seventeen one viral article added a submarine and even a hoverboard to the list.

32
00:01:56,533 --> 00:02:04,672
One writer searched the phrase and found hundreds of thousands of pages, most of them in favour of ancient flight.

33
00:02:04,672 --> 00:02:06,243
The exhibit is famous.

34
00:02:06,243 --> 00:02:07,599
Now, is it genuine?

35
00:02:08,066 --> 00:02:16,260
In February nineteen ninety eight, a Belgian U F O researcher named Thierry Wathelet decided to find out.

36
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:21,566
He emailed about fifty Egyptologists and museum curators, and asked.

37
00:02:22,033 --> 00:02:25,087
Examination one: is the photograph honest?

38
00:02:25,087 --> 00:02:30,033
A document lab always checks the copy before it checks the original.

39
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:36,913
The first reply came within hours, from Peter Der Manuelian at Boston's Museum of Fine Arts.

40
00:02:36,913 --> 00:02:43,466
What you are looking at, he wrote, is hieroglyphs that have been digitally altered by someone.

41
00:02:43,933 --> 00:02:47,634
Another expert, Jacques Kinnaer, spotted the giveaway.

42
00:02:47,634 --> 00:02:51,952
On the temple, the signs are sunken relief, cut into the stone.

43
00:02:51,952 --> 00:02:56,133
In the famous close-up, they look raised, almost like bronze.

44
00:02:56,599 --> 00:03:02,607
And the helicopter in that close-up does not quite match the same sign in untouched photos.

45
00:03:02,607 --> 00:03:07,426
Its outline has been cleaned up, its edges sharpened, its gaps filled in.

46
00:03:07,426 --> 00:03:13,632
Later, versions shown on television were retouched again, to make the craft even more obvious.

47
00:03:13,632 --> 00:03:16,933
Each copy drifted a little further from the stone.

48
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:20,733
So the most famous picture is a retouched picture.

49
00:03:20,733 --> 00:03:26,533
But this is where honest investigators slow down, because the story does not end there.

50
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,710
Plenty of tourists have photographed the beam with ordinary cameras.

51
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:35,105
The strange shapes are really there in the stone.

52
00:03:35,105 --> 00:03:36,906
The edit exaggerated them.

53
00:03:36,906 --> 00:03:38,499
It did not invent them.

54
00:03:38,966 --> 00:03:44,400
Finding one: the viral image is doctored, and that is a point against the claim.

55
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:48,339
But a doctored copy does not prove the original is boring.

56
00:03:48,339 --> 00:03:51,463
A real carving still needs a real explanation.

57
00:03:51,463 --> 00:03:55,266
So we leave the photographs, and go to the stone itself.

58
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:58,289
Examination two: chain of custody.

59
00:03:58,289 --> 00:04:01,596
Where exactly is this beam, and who made it?

60
00:04:01,596 --> 00:04:06,633
It sits in the Temple of Seti the First, at Abydos, in Upper Egypt.

61
00:04:07,099 --> 00:04:13,551
Seti the First ruled Egypt from about twelve ninety four to twelve seventy nine B C.

62
00:04:13,551 --> 00:04:20,233
His temple at Abydos was built to honour Osiris, god of the dead, and the king himself.

63
00:04:20,699 --> 00:04:25,441
Its inner reliefs are some of the finest carving anywhere in Egypt.

64
00:04:25,441 --> 00:04:29,899
Fine lines, delicate faces, colour still clinging to the stone.

65
00:04:30,366 --> 00:04:33,706
But Seti died before the temple was finished.

66
00:04:33,706 --> 00:04:40,533
The job passed to his son, the most famous builder in Egyptian history: Ramesses the Second.

67
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,934
Ramesses ruled for about sixty six years, and few kings ever built more.

68
00:04:45,934 --> 00:04:56,899
At Abydos he finished the outer courts and the hypostyle halls, the forests of columns at the front of the temple, and he made sure his own name was everywhere.

69
00:04:57,366 --> 00:05:06,835
And that is where our exhibit lives: on an architrave, a stone beam resting on top of the columns in the first hypostyle hall.

70
00:05:06,835 --> 00:05:09,766
Part of the section Ramesses completed.

71
00:05:10,233 --> 00:05:13,218
Scholars note his work there was hurried.

72
00:05:13,218 --> 00:05:18,095
Doorways were blocked, the plan was trimmed, the decoration rushed.

73
00:05:18,095 --> 00:05:22,899
Egyptologists even have a nickname for him: Ramesses the Chiseler.

74
00:05:23,366 --> 00:05:25,932
Custody since then is well documented.

75
00:05:25,932 --> 00:05:36,533
The temple was cleared in the eighteen sixties, then photographed and copied in detail by an expedition that published four volumes by nineteen thirty three.

76
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:43,746
As one Egyptologist put it, the temple has been intensely studied, copied and published.

77
00:05:43,746 --> 00:05:46,276
No unusual hieroglyphs are known.

78
00:05:46,276 --> 00:05:48,500
So what is going on up there?

79
00:05:48,966 --> 00:05:50,991
Examination three: two hands.

80
00:05:50,991 --> 00:05:57,833
In a document lab, one of the first questions is whether a page was written once, or written over.

81
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:02,577
There is a word for a surface written on twice: a palimpsest.

82
00:06:02,577 --> 00:06:10,500
Medieval scribes scraped old parchment and reused it, and centuries later the first text can still bleed through.

83
00:06:10,966 --> 00:06:14,100
Egyptian builders did the same thing in stone.

84
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:20,233
When a new king took over a monument, he often replaced the old king's names with his own.

85
00:06:20,699 --> 00:06:24,516
In Seti's temple, that is exactly what happened.

86
00:06:24,516 --> 00:06:30,797
Ramesses had his father's royal titles on this beam replaced by his own titles.

87
00:06:30,797 --> 00:06:31,592
Same spot.

88
00:06:31,592 --> 00:06:32,466
Same stone.

89
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:36,314
Now look at the helicopter with that in mind.

90
00:06:36,314 --> 00:06:45,933
According to Egyptologist Peter Brand, it is made from a bow sign from Seti's text, and two arm signs from the text of Ramesses.

91
00:06:46,399 --> 00:06:53,120
Put the two layers on top of each other, and the strokes of one king's words cross the strokes of the other's.

92
00:06:53,120 --> 00:07:03,566
The rotor, the cabin and the tail are pieces of two different sentences, written about twenty years apart, by two different teams of carvers who never meant them to touch.

93
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:14,896
Another Egyptologist, Eugene Cruz Uribe, pointed to the signs for the number nine and for foreign lands, carved one over the other, with parts lost.

94
00:07:14,896 --> 00:07:18,566
The tank and submarine come from the same overlap.

95
00:07:19,033 --> 00:07:24,646
Finding two: two different hands, two different reigns, about thirteen hundred B C.

96
00:07:24,646 --> 00:07:28,366
The shapes are real, but each stroke belongs to a word.

97
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:30,952
Examination four: the filler.

98
00:07:30,952 --> 00:07:36,066
If Ramesses carved over his father's words, why can we still see both?

99
00:07:36,533 --> 00:07:38,000
The method was simple.

100
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,066
The old sunken signs were packed with plaster.

101
00:07:41,066 --> 00:07:47,333
When it set, the surface was smooth again, ready to be carved and painted with the new titles.

102
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:50,309
Painted over, the trick was invisible.

103
00:07:50,309 --> 00:07:57,377
Visitors in Ramesses' day would have looked up and seen one clean, colourful inscription, and nothing else.

104
00:07:57,377 --> 00:08:02,133
The father's words were still there, but sealed under a skin of plaster.

105
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,724
Then came three thousand years.

106
00:08:04,724 --> 00:08:05,546
Paint faded.

107
00:08:05,546 --> 00:08:07,464
Parts of the roof collapsed.

108
00:08:07,464 --> 00:08:09,999
Weather and time worked on the stone.

109
00:08:10,466 --> 00:08:12,979
And the plaster began to fall out.

110
00:08:12,979 --> 00:08:19,704
Wherever it dropped away, Seti's original signs reappeared underneath Ramesses' newer ones.

111
00:08:19,704 --> 00:08:21,699
Both texts showing at once.

112
00:08:22,166 --> 00:08:23,909
This is not a one-off.

113
00:08:23,909 --> 00:08:31,513
Across the hypostyle hall, column after column shows the names of Seti and Ramesses overlapping.

114
00:08:31,513 --> 00:08:36,266
On one, Ramesses even reversed the direction of the writing.

115
00:08:36,733 --> 00:08:46,074
Aidan Dodson, of the University of Bristol, summed it up: the plaster has fallen out, leaving images that look rather like modern items.

116
00:08:46,074 --> 00:08:51,500
A Copenhagen scholar called it a perfectly clear case of an ancient correction.

117
00:08:51,966 --> 00:09:01,950
Add erosion of the stone surface, which is visible elsewhere in the temple too, and edges soften into outlines our brains are eager to complete.

118
00:09:01,950 --> 00:09:05,833
Finding three: the filler failed, and time did the rest.

119
00:09:06,299 --> 00:09:08,385
Examination five: the reading.

120
00:09:08,385 --> 00:09:10,541
Hieroglyphs are not decoration.

121
00:09:10,541 --> 00:09:17,563
They are a full writing system with grammar, spelling and fixed formulas, read by scholars every day.

122
00:09:17,563 --> 00:09:22,499
So if we read this beam like any other text, what does it actually say?

123
00:09:22,966 --> 00:09:25,383
Every pharaoh had five official names.

124
00:09:25,383 --> 00:09:32,633
One of them is called the Two Ladies name, after the vulture goddess and the cobra goddess who protected the king.

125
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:38,394
Architraves like this one usually carry those royal names, in a fixed order.

126
00:09:38,394 --> 00:09:43,966
And every one of the so called flying machines sits inside the Two Ladies names.

127
00:09:44,433 --> 00:09:51,260
Seti's original read, in translation: Powerful of scimitar, who suppresses the Nine Bows.

128
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:56,399
The Nine Bows were Egypt's traditional enemies, bows as in archery.

129
00:09:56,866 --> 00:10:02,666
Ramesses' replacement read: protector of Egypt, who repels foreign lands.

130
00:10:02,666 --> 00:10:04,970
A boast written over a boast.

131
00:10:04,970 --> 00:10:13,233
Then each text ends with the king's throne name: Menmaatra for Seti, User maatra Setepenra for Ramesses.

132
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:16,983
This reading is not a guess from the internet.

133
00:10:16,983 --> 00:10:26,833
It is set out by Egyptologist Joshua Roberson in a twenty sixteen article, and by Peter Brand in his twenty twenty three book on Ramesses.

134
00:10:27,299 --> 00:10:34,386
Another scholar, Katherine Griffis Greenberg, even gave page numbers in a standard handbook of royal names.

135
00:10:34,386 --> 00:10:37,366
The kind of reference you can check yourself.

136
00:10:37,833 --> 00:10:40,447
So the helicopter has a translation.

137
00:10:40,447 --> 00:10:44,005
It reads, roughly, Nine Bows meets foreign lands.

138
00:10:44,005 --> 00:10:48,000
Finding four: the exhibit is a sentence, not a picture.

139
00:10:48,466 --> 00:10:51,248
Examination six: comparison specimens.

140
00:10:51,248 --> 00:10:56,957
A forger's document often fails when you compare it with everything around it.

141
00:10:56,957 --> 00:10:58,933
So, what else should exist?

142
00:10:59,399 --> 00:11:09,744
If Egyptians flew helicopters, we would expect the machinery behind them: metal workshops, engines, fuel, spare parts, landing places, crash sites.

143
00:11:09,744 --> 00:11:13,544
Egypt is one of the most excavated countries on Earth.

144
00:11:13,544 --> 00:11:15,866
Archaeology has found none of it.

145
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:21,647
Egyptian texts boast about everything: chariots, ships, gold, victories.

146
00:11:21,647 --> 00:11:23,714
Not one boasts about flight.

147
00:11:23,714 --> 00:11:27,183
And no other tomb or temple shows a helicopter.

148
00:11:27,183 --> 00:11:30,799
Only this one beam, and only at this one overlap.

149
00:11:31,266 --> 00:11:35,263
There is a name for what our eyes are doing: pareidolia.

150
00:11:35,263 --> 00:11:39,974
The same instinct that finds faces in clouds and electric sockets.

151
00:11:39,974 --> 00:11:43,899
It is a feature of the brain, not a flaw of the viewer.

152
00:11:44,366 --> 00:11:45,814
Then there is context.

153
00:11:45,814 --> 00:11:51,538
This temple was built to join the dead king with Osiris, so that he would live forever.

154
00:11:51,538 --> 00:11:54,763
Its walls are prayers, offerings and royal names.

155
00:11:54,763 --> 00:12:04,633
A royal title is the last place a scribe would slip in a picture of a vehicle, and nobody in three thousand years of visitors wrote that they saw one.

156
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,630
And the alien version?

157
00:12:06,630 --> 00:12:13,726
It needs visitors who left one doodle in a dead king's name, and nothing else in three thousand years.

158
00:12:13,726 --> 00:12:15,186
That is not evidence.

159
00:12:15,186 --> 00:12:17,899
It is an overlap with a story attached.

160
00:12:18,366 --> 00:12:19,240
Lab report.

161
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:22,100
Time to score the Abydos helicopter.

162
00:12:22,566 --> 00:12:26,255
A real carved beam in Seti's temple: evidence.

163
00:12:26,255 --> 00:12:31,308
Craft-like shapes in untouched photos: real, and a coincidence.

164
00:12:31,308 --> 00:12:35,077
Seti's titles under Ramesses' titles: evidence.

165
00:12:35,077 --> 00:12:38,766
Plaster that fell out, plus erosion: evidence.

166
00:12:39,233 --> 00:12:41,771
The famous viral photo: retouched.

167
00:12:41,771 --> 00:12:44,682
Any supporting trace of aircraft: none.

168
00:12:44,682 --> 00:12:47,966
Ancient flight, or alien visitors: debunked.

169
00:12:48,433 --> 00:12:49,326
The verdict.

170
00:12:49,326 --> 00:12:50,591
Not a helicopter.

171
00:12:50,591 --> 00:13:03,166
Exhibit A is a genuine document that was edited twice: once by a king in about twelve seventy nine B C, and once by someone with photo software in the nineteen nineties.

172
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:14,430
Somewhere, about three thousand three hundred years ago, a carver working for Ramesses smoothed his plaster over an old king's words and never imagined they would come back.

173
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:14,991
They did.

174
00:13:14,991 --> 00:13:17,862
And by pure chance, they look like the future.

175
00:13:17,862 --> 00:13:23,666
That is the real mystery of Abydos: not a lost aircraft, but how hungry our eyes are for one.

176
00:13:24,133 --> 00:13:28,613
Next case: stone walls in Scotland that were melted into glass.

177
00:13:28,613 --> 00:13:31,600
Ancient lasers, or something much simpler?

178
00:13:32,066 --> 00:13:33,758
What do you see in the beam?

179
00:13:33,758 --> 00:13:38,833
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
